                <mxCell id="5" value="&lt;h1&gt;Turnouts&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Problem: A turnout can have 2 to N positions, though generally at most 4. Though if we want something like a turntable or a transfer table to be considered as a turnout then we could have N positions. So this leads also to that a turnout driver could be the same though generally a turnout driver will not have more positions than a turnout but technically could be a posibility. With DCC systems they generally treat a turnout as only binary for positions. Also a turnout with 3+ positions (ex: 3 way Y or a single/double slip) could have more than one driver.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;For a regural turnouts that have two positions&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;spacing=5;spacingTop=-20;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
